<title>JAPAN: Honda shares slip on profit taking.</title>
<headline>Honda shares slip on profit taking.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Honda Motor Co Ltd slipped for the first time in five days on Friday morning, weighed down by profit taking, brokers said.</p>
<p>The major automaker's share price was down 60 yen at 4,090 at 0145 GMT, on turnover of 907,000 shares.  </p>
<p>&quot;Blue-chip issues in general softened. The yen's rise pushed buyers to the sidelines and prompted profit taking,&quot; said a trader at a second-tier Japanese securities house.</p>
